A||||10||coyote||Help removing window tint||||5||
Z||000000||coyote||08-01-2000||12:27 PM||||Does anybody out there know of easy way to get tinting material off of a window, started with a razor blade, but that will be forever. any help would be appreciated.<P>TIA<P>Coyote<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-01-2000||12:33 PM||||get a corner started and keep pulling, if it tears get another spot till u get the plastic film off. To get the glue off first try a stong mixture of water and ammonia. Some brands will wash rite off. If it doesnt, go to a Auto parts store that sells tint, GILA now makes a bottle of adhesive remover.<P>rg||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||08-01-2000||12:33 PM||||razor and lots of soapy water||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric_PA||08-01-2000||12:51 PM||||I must say, it is a pain to get off. What I did was first pull all the tint material off. Then I used a rag and some paint thinner on the rag. I just kept rubbing it, and the glue would start to roll up and make a mess along with those fumes. You may not want to use thinner, but it worked for me, you just end up a little lite-headed.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||08-01-2000||01:05 PM||||  The quickest way is with a razor and warm soapy water. I took all of mine off including the bottom side of the sunroof (previous owner was an idiot) in about 45 minutes. The rear window was the worst. Your local auto parts store should have some good razor kits real cheap.<P>Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
Z||000005||86SE||08-01-2000||02:34 PM||||Try taking it off when its cold, in the morning is the best time.  If you get a corner started, the glue and tint will come off in 1 sheet.  Then you can clean the window with some good window cleaner to get what ever glue is left, or take a sharp razor and it will take the glue off very easily.  Thats how I did mine, it took about 10 min and you can't even tell there was tint on there.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000006||coyote||08-02-2000||11:50 AM||||Thanks for all your help guys. I just grabbed a razor blade and scrapped and pulled till it was done, took about 45 minutes for both windows. Used a product galled Goo-Gone to remove adhesive, snd now there good as new.<P>Coyote<BR>84 SE<BR>87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||b lo 0||08-02-2000||12:13 PM||||Goo Gone is great, but it leaves a greasy residue that you have to clean off.  Congrats though, I had to do it on my '79 Camaro and it's a PAIN IN THE BUTT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fret Naught||08-02-2000||12:54 PM||||I have been thinking about taking mine in and having the windows tinted? is there reason not to?||||reg||1
Z||000009||contra||08-02-2000||06:55 PM||||Welcome to the wonderfull world of Varsol, paint thinner, and a razor blade<P>took me an hour but i got that crap off both of my side windows...i wanted to tint mine darker than they were...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||olympic||08-02-2000||10:46 PM||||   I recently pulled the tint off of the front 2 windows on a car I just bought.  I started a corner with the razor and the whole sheet came off real easy.  I bought one of those single edged razors from a hardware store that comes with a little plastic handle that snaps on.  It worked perfect.  I still had to wash the windows several times because they were still slightly tacky and would bind with the dew wipes.<P>Fret Naught,<BR>   You'll want to check on the laws in your area regarding window tinting.  Some placed only allow windows behind the driver to be tinted.  Also, make sure you go to a professional that will give you a warranty against bubbling, peeling and "purpling".  A pro job will last for a long time.  One of my cars was done 10 years ago and it still looks perfect.||||reg||1
